Finish Cookie AutoDelete parity: all-sites mode, a greylist, and a delay.

Three patches already cover most of it - the delete-on-exit toggle, the
keep list, and per-site reset on tab close. What was missing was the model
Cookie AutoDelete actually uses. Its list is a list of sites to KEEP and
everything else goes; ours was a list of sites to DELETE and everything
else stays. Same mechanism, opposite polarity, and the opposite default.

Three additions close it.

All-sites mode (kAeriumEphemeralAllSites, off by default)

  Turns the ephemeral list inside out: every site is cleared when its last
  tab closes, and kAeriumClearOnExitExcludedSites becomes the keep list.
  Expressed with BrowsingDataFilterBuilder::Mode::kPreserve rather than by
  enumerating domains to delete, because the set of domains holding data is
  not knowable from here - and listing it would be far larger than listing
  the handful being spared.

  Off by default deliberately. Turning it on signs the user out of every
  site not on the keep list, which is a thing to opt into, not to receive
  in an update. The explicit list keeps working unchanged when it is off,
  so both models coexist rather than one replacing the other.

  The exclusion list is shared with the on-exit toggle rather than
  duplicated. "Never delete this site's data" is one intent; a second list
  would let the same site be kept at shutdown and wiped on tab close, which
  nobody means.

  Three things are spared in this mode: the keep list because the user said
  so, the greylist because it survives until shutdown and this is not
  shutdown, and whatever is still open - clearing a site out from under a
  tab displaying it logs the user out mid-session. The explicit-list path
  always protected open sites; this path needs it more, since every site is
  now a candidate.

Greylist (kAeriumSessionOnlySites)

  Cookie AutoDelete's middle tier: keep this site while the browser runs,
  drop it at shutdown. Between "never delete" and "delete the moment the
  last tab closes", and it covers the ordinary case of a site you want to
  stay signed into while you work but not tomorrow.

  Cleared by its own removal at shutdown, before every condition in
  ClearBrowsingDataForOnExitPolicy() and outside all of them. Session-only
  is a promise made per site, not a mode: it should not require asking for
  a general clean-out, and turning that clean-out off should not cancel it.

Delay (kAeriumEphemeralDelaySeconds, default 10)

  Not a nicety. Sign-in flows routinely bounce through a provider in a tab
  that closes itself, and OAuth popups close the moment they hand back a
  token - clearing the instant the tab count reaches zero can delete the
  cookie the redirect is about to need. It also forgives closing a tab by
  accident. Cookie AutoDelete ships a delay for the same reasons.

  Implemented by making the existing post-a-task hop a delayed one rather
  than adding a timer. The weak pointer already in use is the cancellation
  mechanism: Shutdown() invalidates the factory, so a pending clear never
  runs against a half-destroyed profile. Clamped to 0-3600 in the browser
  and again in the UI - the first stops a hand-edited Preferences file from
  silently disabling the feature with a negative or enormous value, the
  second stops a type="number" field reporting an empty string mid-edit
  from being persisted as 0, which reads as "clear immediately".

AeriumEphemeralDomains() becomes AeriumDomainsFromPref(), taking the pref
name, because four lists now share that shape - ephemeral, keep, greylist
and the on-exit exclusions - and they have to agree on what counts as one
site or a domain could end up both kept and deleted.

Still to do, tracked rather than silently skipped: the greylist has no
Settings list of its own yet (the pref is live and settings_private can
reach it), and none of the three earlier patches or this one exists on
Android.
